  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "In Chefland, there are NNN cities (numbered 111 through NNN) connected by N−1N-1N−1 bidirectional roads. Each city has exactly one garden. For each valid iii, let's denote the population of the iii-th city by AiA_iAi​ and the initial number of fruits in its garden by BiB_iBi​; also, at any time, let's denote the current number of fruits in its garden by FiF_iFi​ (Fi=BiF_i = B_iFi​=Bi​ initially).\n\nYou are given a permutation PPP of the integers 111 through NNN. For each iii (1≤i≤N1 \\le i \\le N1≤i≤N), during the iii-th of the next NNN days, the people of the city PiP_iPi​ do the following:\n\n\nFor each city jjj which is reachable from the city PiP_iPi​ (including the city PiP_iPi​ itself), visit the city jjj and consume min(APi,Fj)\\mathrm{min}(A_{P_i}, F_j)min(APi​​,Fj​) fruits from the garden of the city jjj; afterwards, FjF_jFj​ decreases by min(APi,Fj)\\mathrm{min}(A_{P_i}, F_j)min(APi​​,Fj​).\nReturn to the city PiP_iPi​ and cut off all the roads that are connecting it to other cities, so that nobody can visit the city PiP_iPi​ or visit any other city from their city if it requires passing through the city PiP_iPi​.\nFor each valid iii, let DiD_iDi​ be the first day when the number of fruits in the iii-th city's garden becomes zero, or −1-1−1 if the fruits in its garden never end up all eaten. Find D1,D2,…,DND_1, D_2, \\ldots, D_ND1​,D2​,…,DN​.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1051 \\le T \\le 10^51≤T≤105",
      "1≤N≤2⋅1051 \\le N \\le 2 \\cdot 10^51≤N≤2⋅105",
      "1≤u,v≤N1 \\le u, v \\le N1≤u,v≤N",
      "1≤Pi≤N1 \\le P_i \\le N1≤Pi​≤N for each valid iii",
      "1≤Ai,Bi≤1091 \\le A_i, B_i \\le 10^91≤Ai​,Bi​≤109 for each valid iii",
      "the sum of NNN over all test cases does not exceed 5⋅1055 \\cdot 10^55⋅105",
      "Subtasks**Subtask #1 (30 points):**",
      "N≤103N \\le 10^3N≤103",
      "the sum of NNN over all test cases does not exceed 5⋅1035 \\cdot 10^35⋅103"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "The first line of the input contains a single integer TTT denoting the number of test cases. The description of TTT test cases follows.\nThe first line of each test case contains a single integer NNN.\nEach of the next N−1N-1N−1 lines contains two space-separated integers uuu and vvv denoting that vertices uuu and vvv are connected by an edge.\nThe next line contains NNN space-separated integers P1,P2,…,PNP_1, P_2, \\ldots, P_NP1​,P2​,…,PN​.\nThe next line contains NNN space-separated integers A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​.\nThe last line contains NNN space-separated integers B1,B2,…,BNB_1, B_2, \\ldots, B_NB1​,B2​,…,BN​.",
    "outputFormat": "For each test case, print a single line containing NNN space-separated integers D1,D2,…,DND_1, D_2, \\ldots, D_ND1​,D2​,…,DN​.",
    "notes": [],
