        "explanation": "Explanation:\nExample case 1: The process is as follows:\n\nOn day 111, people from city 111 eat 111 fruit from each garden. Afterwards, there are [0,2,5][0, 2, 5][0,2,5] fruits in the gardens of cities [1,2,3][1, 2, 3][1,2,3] respectively, so the answer for city 111 is 111, since the number of fruits in this garden becomes zero on day 111.\nThen, on day 222, people from city 222 eat 222 fruits from each of the gardens in cities 222 and 333. Afterwards, there are 000 fruits in the garden of city 222 (so the answer for city 222 is 222, since the number of fruits in this garden becomes zero on this day) and 333 fruits in the garden of city 333.\nFinally, on day 333, people from city 333 eat 333 fruits from the garden of city 333, so the answer for city 333 is 333."
